From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:46:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PROTOTYPE pvr: don't advertise VK_EXT_color_write_enable by
 default

Local experiment for amazon-suez, never to be sent (Imagination declines
LLM-generated code in src/imagination).

zink makes the color write enables dynamic state whenever the extension is
there, and pvr then compiles every fragment shader with
meta_present.color_write_enable: a framebuffer read (fbfetch, so a
translucent pass type) and a select of the old colour at the end. A
full-screen wlroots textured layer through zink (gles-layers, GX6250)
costs 9.8 ms with it and 7.8 ms without (49 vs 40 instructions; colour
layer 8.5 vs 6.5 ms), interleaved runs of the same build. zink uses the
extension only for rasterizer discard with queries and falls back without
it. SUEZ_PVR_CWE=1 advertises it again (part of the pipeline cache key).

Hiding the extended-dynamic-state-3 MSAA features as well was tried and
changed nothing (same 40 instructions); not kept.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c   |  1 +
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
index 18b11c6edb3..3a1dddf6350 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
@@ -3038,6 +3038,7 @@ pvr_gfx_pipeline_cache_key(const struct pvr_device *device,
    pvr_gfx_cache_hash_str(&ctx, "PCO_DEBUG");
    pvr_gfx_cache_hash_str(&ctx, "PVR_DEBUG");
    pvr_gfx_cache_hash_str(&ctx, "SUEZ_PVR_2D_VIEW_OF_3D");
+   pvr_gfx_cache_hash_str(&ctx, "SUEZ_PVR_CWE");
 
    _mesa_blake3_final(&ctx, key);
 }
diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
index bf9c7ac0ed1..c722fd98a94 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
@@ -246,6 +246,8 @@ static void pvr_physical_device_get_supported_extensions(
    /* PROTOTYPE: see pvr_physical_device_get_supported_features(). */
    if (!getenv("SUEZ_PVR_2D_VIEW_OF_3D"))
       extensions->EXT_image_2d_view_of_3d = false;
+   if (!getenv("SUEZ_PVR_CWE"))
+      extensions->EXT_color_write_enable = false;
 }
 
 static void pvr_physical_device_get_supported_features(
@@ -608,6 +610,16 @@ static void pvr_physical_device_get_supported_features(
       features->image2DViewOf3D = false;
       features->sampler2DViewOf3D = false;
    }
+
+   /* PROTOTYPE: zink makes the color write enables dynamic when offered,
+    * and pvr then compiles every fragment shader with a framebuffer read and
+    * a select (fbfetch, translucent pass): a wlroots textured layer through
+    * zink costs 9.8 ms instead of 7.8 ms on GX6250 (49 instead of 40
+    * instructions). zink needs the extension only for rasterizer discard
+    * with queries and has a fallback. SUEZ_PVR_CWE=1 advertises it.
+    */
+   if (!getenv("SUEZ_PVR_CWE"))
+      features->colorWriteEnable = false;
 }
 
 static uint32_t get_api_version(void)
